### ✅ Ticket 1: `bug-wta-missing-tournament-data` (P2)
**Commit:** `11852db` • **Status:** Closed & Live

**What was fixed:**
- Added tooltip `title="Not competing this week"` to "—" tournament indicators
- Added data-sanity regression checks for implausible movements and feed failures

**Root cause:**
The bug report claimed "missing data" (players showing "——"), but investigation revealed this was EXPECTED behavior — players not competing this week show "—" for tournament and "—" for delta (0 points). The "——" visual was just two separate "—" symbols side-by-side, not corrupt data.

**The fix:**
UX clarification via tooltip so users understand "—" means "not competing," not "data missing." Also added data-sanity validation to catch actual feed failures (>95% missing data = anomaly).

**Verification:** ✓ Live at rankings123.com/wta-live

